<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation (Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets))",
        "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation faithfully reproduces Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 68.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-allometric-compound-leaf-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D finite-element adaxial-abaxial lamina thickness mechanics, cell division, or vascular bundle differentiation inside the rachis",
        "does_not_claim: Emergent auxin convergence-point patterning (PIN1 up-the-gradient transport is not solved; tooth number and spacing are inputs)",
        "does_not_claim: Realised cell-scale growth anisotropy from microtubule stress feedback (a_lamina = 0.0 by default; the vein-axis channel yields a 1.04 axial stretch ratio)",
        "does_not_claim: Reproduction of Cardamine hirsuta leaflet-level dissection (I_D 0.785) or of the mir164a-4 / rco benchmark ordering",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated excess-green chromatic + Euclidean distance-transform segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Cardamine hirsuta botanical specimen (32 compound leaflet lobes, perimeter dissection ratio 4.0939, radial tip-to-sinus dissection index 0.5202 +- 0.0128 SE) — unchanged from v2",
        "reconstructed_in_script: EMERGENT integrated margin contour (`integrate_margin_outgrowth`, radial proximodistal growth + outward normal term) with emergent radial dissection index: cuc2-1 0.000 (ref 0.012), cuc2-1D 0.000 (ref 0.025), At WT 0.230 (calibration datum 0.228), Ch rco 0.219 (ref 0.312), mir164a-4 0.233 (ref 0.445), Ch WT 0.254 (ref 0.785); 6-genotype Pearson r = 0.807 (p = 0.052, RMSE 0.237); stages P3-P6 I_D 0.000 / 0.168 / 0.219 / 0.256 with 1/3/5/7 peaks; eta x growth-duration sweep ceiling 0.427",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Growing 2D cellular spring-lattice lamina (441 vertices, 804 triangles, bilaterally symmetric) with screened-Poisson growth field, procambial midvein, Mitchison-canalized lateral veins (4/4 At WT, 6/6 Ch WT, 0 cuc2-1 drained to the midvein), vein-axis microtubule anisotropy a_vein = 0.20 (ablation run a = 0): mesh I_D 0.117 (At), 0.131 (Ch), 0.000 (cuc2-1), 0.102 (Ch, MT off); 0 inverted elements; max residual force 1e-3; realised vein-axial stretch ratio 1.04",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Prescribed-template margin Auxin/CUC2 profile (convergence peaks are Gaussian inputs, L198-216) with Loop 1 / Loop 2 / Loop 3 algebraic identities verified exactly (Law 1 residual 5.7e-14, Law 2 residual 0.0, Law 3 identity 0.0) and strong Auxin-CUC2 antiphase (r = -0.991)",
        "reported_in_source: Bilsborough et al. (2011) PNAS 108:3424-3429 interconnected leaf margin feedback loops: Loop 1 (CUC2 promotes PIN1 up-the-gradient polarization rho_{ij} propto (1 + gamma_CUC2 C_i) exp(beta A_j)), Loop 2 (Auxin represses CUC2 transcription C_i = C_max / (1 + (A_i/K_A)^n)), Loop 3 (differential normal margin outgrowth v_n(s) = v_0 [A(s)^m/(K_g^m+A(s)^m)] (1 - eta_sinus C(s)) with intercalary tooth insertion)",
        "reported_in_source: Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. B 207:79-109 flux-feedback canalization; Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev 20:1015-1027 marginal convergence points initiate vein strands; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 / Sampathkumar et al. (2014) eLife 3:e01967 microtubule-aligned anisotropic wall reinforcement",
        "reported_in_source: Vlad et al. (2014) Science 343:780-783 and Kierzkowski et al. (2019) Cell 177:1405-1418: local sinus growth repression by RCO in Cardamine hirsuta converts shallow serrations into deeply incised compound leaflets; growth-based framework with polarity-aligned anisotropic growth",
        "transfer_boundary: 1D prescribed-template epidermal margin signal -> 2D integrated margin contour and 2D growing cellular spring-lattice lamina (reduced-dimensional stand-in for the requested 3D FE vertex mesh); 2D botanical specimen contour morphometrics on a whole rosette canopy, not a single leaf" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Spirals, Veins & Puzzle Cells" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Golden Angle / Auxin Flux" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Cardamine" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py; output: docs/media/allometric_compound_leaf_comparison.png; organism: Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, lean 4.35.0; spec_fingerprint: f2deb6d5b7f7613348124ac9cf34bbeb431e1d1f13eac9c5772c32d01ccc0fba; artifact_sha256: 4ac058048dd650b246bc2e4bb020b667700ab266be113dacd5722e2e338d3a11; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/allometric_compound_leaf_reference.json=fa4f9b265dd83379..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/cardamine_hirsuta_compound_leaf_specimen.jpg=1c268fecb3660b31..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/paper_citations.bib=8323f1f35f2613d6..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/scout_manifest.json=46ea1539febdb312...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-allometric-compound-leaf-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Bilsborough et al. (2011) PNAS 108:3424-3429 interconnected leaf margin feedback loops: Loop 1 (CUC2 promotes PIN1 up-the-gradient polarization rho_{ij} propto (1 + gamma_CUC2 C_i) exp(beta A_j)), Loop 2 (Auxin represses CUC2 transcription C_i = C_max / (1 + (A_i/K_A)^n)), Loop 3 (differential normal margin outgrowth v_n(s) = v_0 [A(s)^m/(K_g^m+A(s)^m)] (1 - eta_sinus C(s)) with intercalary tooth insertion) | Vlad et al. (2014) Science 343:780-783 and Kierzkowski et al. (2019) Cell 177:1405-1418: local sinus growth repression by RCO in Cardamine hirsuta converts shallow serrations into deeply incised compound leaflets; growth-based framework with polarity-aligned anisotropic growth | Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. B 207:79-109 flux-feedback canalization; Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev 20:1015-1027 marginal convergence points initiate vein strands; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 / Sampathkumar et al. (2014) eLife 3:e01967 microtubule-aligned anisotropic wall reinforcement; reconstructed_in_script: Prescribed-template margin Auxin/CUC2 profile (convergence peaks are Gaussian inputs, L198-216) with Loop 1 / Loop 2 / Loop 3 algebraic identities verified exactly (Law 1 residual 5.7e-14, Law 2 residual 0.0, Law 3 identity 0.0) and strong Auxin-CUC2 antiphase (r = -0.991) | EMERGENT integrated margin contour (`integrate_margin_outgrowth`, radial proximodistal growth + outward normal term) with emergent radial dissection index: cuc2-1 0.000 (ref 0.012), cuc2-1D 0.000 (ref 0.025), At WT 0.230 (calibration datum 0.228), Ch rco 0.219 (ref 0.312), mir164a-4 0.233 (ref 0.445), Ch WT 0.254 (ref 0.785); 6-genotype Pearson r = 0.807 (p = 0.052, RMSE 0.237); stages P3-P6 I_D 0.000 / 0.168 / 0.219 / 0.256 with 1/3/5/7 peaks; eta x growth-duration sweep ceiling 0.427 | Growing 2D cellular spring-lattice lamina (441 vertices, 804 triangles, bilaterally symmetric) with screened-Poisson growth field, procambial midvein, Mitchison-canalized lateral veins (4/4 At WT, 6/6 Ch WT, 0 cuc2-1 drained to the midvein), vein-axis microtubule anisotropy a_vein = 0.20 (ablation run a = 0): mesh I_D 0.117 (At), 0.131 (Ch), 0.000 (cuc2-1), 0.102 (Ch, MT off); 0 inverted elements; max residual force 1e-3; realised vein-axial stretch ratio 1.04 | Automated excess-green chromatic + Euclidean distance-transform segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Cardamine hirsuta botanical specimen (32 compound leaflet lobes, perimeter dissection ratio 4.0939, radial tip-to-sinus dissection index 0.5202 +- 0.0128 SE) — unchanged from v2; transfer_boundary: 1D prescribed-template epidermal margin signal -> 2D integrated margin contour and 2D growing cellular spring-lattice lamina (reduced-dimensional stand-in for the requested 3D FE vertex mesh); 2D botanical specimen contour morphometrics on a whole rosette canopy, not a single leaf; does_not_claim: 3D finite-element adaxial-abaxial lamina thickness mechanics, cell division, or vascular bundle differentiation inside the rachis | Emergent auxin convergence-point patterning (PIN1 up-the-gradient transport is not solved; tooth number and spacing are inputs) | Reproduction of Cardamine hirsuta leaflet-level dissection (I_D 0.785) or of the mir164a-4 / rco benchmark ordering | Realised cell-scale growth anisotropy from microtubule stress feedback (a_lamina = 0.0 by default; the vein-axis channel yields a 1.04 axial stretch ratio)]" ;
    pk1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2019.05.011>,
