<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-80) maps all five laws to their Lean theorems with verified line loci and states the Pass 3 changes, the honest outcome and the model's limits; `GrowingLaminaSpringMesh` and the new helpers carry per-step citations (Mitchison, Scarpella, Hamant, Sampathkumar, Kierzkowski); the math-KG yaml (`przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.yaml`, 5 equations) has lean_locus and code_locus entries that were re-checked against the current file. Deductions: several docstrings and the Section 2 header still call the prescribed-template margin signal a \"reaction-transport PDE\" (L154-186) (-8); v2 line references elsewhere in the repository (v2 audit, KG) now point at shifted lines (-4); panel titles in the growth GIF still read as validation rather than template output (-4); mesh parameter defaults are documented only in the signature, not in the docstring (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L154–L186: simulate_growing_margin_feedback_pde is still documented as a reaction-transport PDE although its peaks are a Gaussian template (see HONESTY NOTE L187) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L154-L186>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Loops 1-3 of Bilsborough et al. (2011) are implemented as exact algebraic laws on a 1D margin profile (L154-317), the margin contour is now genuinely integrated from the Loop 3 outgrowth velocity (`integrate_margin_outgrowth`, L417-475; emergent I_D L476-523) and the new `GrowingLaminaSpringMesh` (L654-1137) is a real overdamped elastic solver (Hookean springs + area penalty, L999-1025) with rest-length growth from an anisotropic tensor (L1027-1065), a screened-Poisson growth field (L872-887), Mitchison canalization on sparse linear solves (L905-927) and a flux-connected vein topology check (L929-947); 5 Lean 4 theorems (3 v2 + Hamant partition L164-192 + Mitchison feedback L206-224) mirror the code. Deductions: the auxin convergence peaks are a prescribed Gaussian template (L198-216; disclosed L187-194), so Loop 1 is verified only as an identity and tooth number/spacing are inputs (-10); the remediation asked for a 3D FE vertex mesh and the delivered lamina is 2D, without thickness, division or adaxial/abaxial layers (-8); the stress-feedback lamina anisotropy is implemented (L985-990) but disabled by default (a_lamina = 0.0, L706) because it destabilised the explicit relaxation (-5); the equal-duration growth law cannot produce leaflet-level dissection (sweep ceiling 0.427, L1186-1215) (-5)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L187–L216: HONESTY NOTE and convergence_drive: auxin peaks are prescribed Gaussians at u = +-0.22 k; PIN1 up-the-gradient transport is not solved <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L187-L216>",
        "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L705–L706: a_vein = 0.20 but a_lamina = 0.0: the Sampathkumar (2014) stress-feedback channel is switched off by default <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L705-L706>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation — Morphometric validation: 55/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1339-1570) returns 20 measurements, every one with unit, reference_value, reference_source, uncertainty and method; all dissection indices are emergent and the circular Pass 2 r = 0.998 is explicitly withdrawn (L1426-1434). Lean-mirrored identities (L1216-1249) and mesh-validity metrics (inverted elements 0, residual 1e-3) are included. Deductions: At WT is a calibration (kappa_n tuned to 0.228, L426), not a prediction (-5); Ch WT misses by 0.53, mir164a-4 by 0.21 and the rco/At WT order is inverted, so the only free predictions fail (-15); the emergent r = 0.807 has p = 0.052 (-5); the specimen measurements' references are self-referential (-7); the MT-ablation effect (delta I_D 0.029) and the vein-axial stretch ratio (1.04 vs 1.02 control) are within the resolution-limit noise of a one-vertex tooth (-8); the `cuc2_mutant_smooth` measurement's reference uncertainty was widened to 0.012 so that 0.000 vs 0.012 passes (-5)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L1415–L1424: cardamine_wt_compound_dissection_index_ID = 0.254 vs reference 0.785 is reported as OUT-OF-PREDICTION rather than fitted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L1415-L1424>",
        "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L426–L427: kappa_n = 0.50 calibrated on the At WT datum: the At WT measurement is a fit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L426-L427>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-measurement-arabidopsis-wt-auxin-cuc2-antiphase-r>,
